y gene RAB34 in four individuals from three unrelated families.","Affected individuals presented a novel form of OFDS (OFDS-RAB34) accompanied by cardiac, cerebral, skeletal and anorectal defects."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"stated for the family"},{"id":"R:37619988:1","pmid":"37619988","label":"Affected fetus","kind":"individual","family":"","n_affected":1,"n_families":1,"sex":"","ancestry":"","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"prenatal","age_last":"fetus","phenotypes":[{"text":"posterior neck edema","hpo_label":"Edema","hpo_id":"HP:0000969","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"micrognathia","hpo_label":"Micrognathia","hpo_id":"HP:0000347","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"low-set ears","hpo_label":"Low-set ears","hpo_id":"HP:0000369","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"small ears","hpo_label":"Small earlobe","hpo_id":"HP:0000385","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"auricular hypoplasia","hpo_label":"Hypoplasia of the ear cartilage","hpo_id":"HP:0100720","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"cleft lip and palate","hpo_label":"Orofacial cleft","hpo_id":"HP:0000202","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"short extremities","hpo_label":"Micromelia","hpo_id":"HP:0002983","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"preaxial polydactyly","hpo_label":"Preaxial polydactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0100258","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"postaxial polydactyly","hpo_label":"Postaxial polydactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0100259","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"RAB34","as_reported":"c.254T>C, p.(Ile85Thr)","cdna":"c.254T>C","protein":"p.(Ile85Thr)","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"inherited","consequence":"missense","key":"V2"},{"gene":"RAB34","as_reported":"c.691C>T, p.(Arg231*)","cdna":"c.691C>T","protein":"p.(Arg231*)","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"inherited","consequence":"nonsense","key":"V3"}],"variant_roles":["causal","causal"],"segregation":"Missense variant maternal, nonsense variant paternal; the unaffected sib carried only the paternal variant","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["The affected fetus had multiple malformations, including posterior neck edema, micrognathia, low-set and small ears, auricular hypoplasia, cleft lip and palate, short extremities, and a combination of rarely occurring pre- and postaxial polydactyly.","Genome sequencing identified compound heterozygous variants in the RAB34 gene: maternal c.254T>C, p.(Ile85Thr), and paternal c.691C>T, p.(Arg231*) variants. Only the paternal variant was present in the unaffected sibling."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:37619988:1","pmid":"37619988","section":"animal_model","statement":"Batkovskyte et al. (2024) noted that Rab34-null mice had been reported in the literature to show a ciliopathy phenotype that included cleft palate and polydactyly. These features matched the malformations in their patient, which supported the pathogenicity of the RAB34 variants they found.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Evidence in the literature indicated that Rab34-/- mice displayed a ciliopathy phenotype with cleft palate and polydactyly. These features were consistent with malformations detected in our patient supporting the pathogenicity of the identified RAB34 variants."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:37384395:1","pmid":"37384395","section":"gene_function","statement":"Bruel et al. (2023) found that the RAB34 variant proteins, clustered near the C terminus, exhibited a strong loss of function; although some variants retained the ability to be recruited to the mother centriole, cells expressing mutant RAB34 showed a significant defect in cilium assembly.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["We find that the protein products of these pathogenic variants, which are clustered near the RAB34 C-terminus, exhibit a strong loss of function.","Although some variants retain the ability to be recruited to the mother centriole, cells expressing mutant RAB34 exhibit a significant defect in cilium assembly."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:37384395:2","pmid":"37384395","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Bruel et al. (2023) noted that RAB34 acts selectively in cell types using the intracellular ciliogenesis pathway, and concluded that RAB34 is the first small GTPase involved in OFDS, with distinct clinical manifestations caused by impairment of intracellular ciliogenesis.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["RAB34 acts selectively in cell types that use the intracellular ciliogenesis pathway, in which nascent cilia begin to form in the cytoplasm.","our studies establish RAB34 as the first small GTPase involved in OFDS and reveal the distinct clinical manifestations caused by impairment of intracellular ciliogenesis."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["RAB34"],"confirmed":["RAB34"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AR"]}